---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import {archive} from '../lib/archive';
---
<Site title="Learning & research overview"><section class="wrap page-head"><p class="kicker">KNOW THE BOUNDARIES</p><h1>Learning & research.</h1><p class="lead">Explore the alphabet and tone marks, then read the preserved pronunciation guidance.</p></section><section class="wrap narrow article-section"><nav class="pills" aria-label="Live language tools"><a href="/learning/alphabet/">Alphabet &amp; tone practice</a><a href="/learning/pronunciation/">Pronunciation references</a></nav><h2>Ifá: the illustrative 16 × 16 model</h2><p>This is a mathematical teaching representation, not authenticated ordering of 256 verses, and not evidence of electronic-computer invention.</p><ol class="odu-list">{archive.oduMainNames.map(name=><li lang="yo">{name}</li>)}</ol><p><a href="/articles/deep-ifa-odu-binary/">Read the original study and its evidence limits →</a></p><p class="notice">Interactive 256-cell model: legacy-only; not implemented in this reading foundation. No verse translations are generated.</p><h2>Pronunciation guidance</h2><p>15 original text entries. Native-speaker recordings are pending; no synthetic or unreviewed audio is supplied.</p><div class="profile-grid">{archive.pronunciationEntries.map(p=><article class="profile"><h3 lang="yo">{p.text}</h3><p>{p.meaning}</p><p class="fine">{p.note}</p><span class="label">Native recording pending</span></article>)}</div><h2>Glossary</h2><dl class="glossary">{archive.glossary.map(g=><div><dt lang="yo">{g.term}</dt><dd>{g.meaning}</dd></div>)}</dl><h2>Other legacy learning tools</h2><p>The original quiz, atlas, timeline, bookmarks and innovation explorer remain in the unchanged root prototype. Their interactive versions are legacy-only in this task.</p><a href="/legacy-links/">Understand the local rollback and legacy links →</a></section></Site>
